Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Jynxzi.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits made.

**The two biggest issues:**

**1. The draft's load-bearing section is factually stale.** "Why Jynxzi Never Left Rainbow Six Siege" argues he stayed in one arena for seven years. He didn't stay — he's been on a Clash Royale grind since late April 2025, and in August 2025 told his own fanbase *"if you only wanna watch me play R6, you're not, like, a real supporter, bro."* By 2026 he's rotating Clash Royale, GTA, Call of Duty, and running his own CS2 tournament. The April 2026 section closes on "he goes home and streams Siege on a controller like nothing happened," which any regular viewer will know is false. The fix isn't just corrective — the exit is the *better* version of the same thesis: the arena-selector eventually walked out of the room he owned and told the holdouts they weren't real supporters.

**2. The Supercell fight is missing, and it's the strongest evidence in his record.** February 2026, Supercell publishes a "Clash Royale: A Historic Year" recap crediting internal decisions and naming zero creators. Jynxzi calls it *"probably the biggest spit in the face I've ever seen,"* MrBeast and CouRageJD back him, and CEO Ilkka Paananen publicly apologizes on Feb 12 for failing to credit creators. The draft's whole argument is that a Three's achievement only becomes worth when a witness confirms it. Here he forced a game company's CEO to confirm it in writing — nothing else in the piece demonstrates the thesis at that scale.

Also flagged: Wembley is overclaimed (match went 10-10 to penalties, his side lost — he was Man of the Match on the losing team, which is the sharper Type 3 detail), the only critic anchor is two years old, and the mother is absent across five separate dad appearances.

Sources: [Sportskeeda — "not a real supporter"](https://www.sportskeeda.com/us/streamers/news-you-re-real-supporter-jynxzi-slams-fans-wanting-play-rainbow-six-siege-pivoting-clash-royale-content), [Dexerto — Supercell](https://www.dexerto.com/gaming/jynxzi-slams-supercell-after-clash-royale-historic-year-recap-omits-his-impact-3317074/), [Dexerto — CEO apology](https://www.dexerto.com/gaming/clash-royale-ceo-apologizes-after-failing-to-credit-jynxzi-3318282/), [Dot Esports — Sidemen 2026](https://dotesports.com/streaming/news/sidemen-charity-match-2026), [Sportskeeda — CS2 tournament backlash](https://www.sportskeeda.com/us/streamers/jynxzi-faces-backlash-inviting-any-actual-counter-strike-2-streamers-upcoming-tournament)
